---
description: Residents can only view record details. No edit and no update status. Staff own those actions.
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Resident view-only records

On parcels, guests, maintenance, and warranties, a resident (`group: "account"`) can open their own record and view the detail.

Residents cannot:

- Edit an existing record (`/edit`, save, or an Edit action)
- Update status (`/status` or a status control)

Those actions are staff-only. Gate them with `isStaffMenuPath()` on the server before the page renders. Hiding the button is not enough.

```tsx
// BAD — resident and staff share the edit page
export default async function EditWarrantyPage() {
  await requireAuth();
  return <WarrantyForm />;
}

// GOOD
const nav = await requireMenuPath("/account/warranties");
if (!isStaffMenuPath(nav, "/account/warranties")) redirect("/account");
```

Profile, Edit Profile, and Additional Information are the resident's own account. This rule does not remove those screens.
